{
  "service": "fcb-reader-excerpt-verification",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "consumers": {
    "reader": {
      "route": "headless:rust",
      "entry": "crates/fcb-source/tests/fcb_012_production.rs",
      "expect": {
        "strings": [
          "escaped \"quotes\"",
          "unicode \u00e9\u4e2d\u6587",
          "surrogate pair \ud83d\ude00"
        ],
        "numbers": [0, -17, 123, 2.5, 1e-10],
        "literals": [true, false, null]
      }
    },
    "fence": {
      "language": "json",
      "capabilities": {
        "string_escapes": "implemented",
        "unicode_sequences": "implemented",
        "numbers": "implemented",
        "structural_punctuation": "implemented",
        "malformed_input": "truthful-tile-no-grammar-claims",
        "dialect_validation": "unsupported"
      },
      "capability_version": "json-lexer/v1"
    }
  },
  "notes": [
    "This fixture is a real consumer document: it exercises strings, escapes,\n    unicode (raw and \\u-escaped), numbers across magnitudes, literals,\n    nesting, and the boundary between lexer truth and parser semantics.",
    "The lexer tiles and classifies; it never claims the document is valid\n    JSON grammar. That distinction is the capability row's whole point."
  ]
}
